{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator attestation for packed-cost AC (classification corrected after completion-verifier feedback). I ran the frozen 40-SHA corpus already recorded on this ticket from unfiltered clone tip d83e9277f420d0135c8e13e67101c53b671edc38. Before corpus: materialize each recorded bindings.json blob oldest-to-newest into a fresh git repo and commit all 40. After corpus: load the same blob at each SHA, remove baseline_advanced_at from every data['bindings'] entry, serialize with the production format json.dump(indent=2, sort_keys=True) plus newline, and commit in the same order into a second fresh repo. For each repo run git repack -Ad --window=250 --depth=50 after commit 1 and after commit 40, stat the single pack, and compute (pack_40-pack_1)/39/1024. Before: pack_1=3,115,474 bytes; pack_40=3,668,053; delta=552,579; marginal=13.84 KiB/version. After: pack_1=3,105,030; pack_40=3,197,938; delta=92,908; marginal=2.33 KiB/version. Ratio=16.8%, which passes the <=25% criterion (and is below 3.20 KiB against the ticket's fixed 12.79 KiB reference). All 40 transformed versions committed distinctly. Scratch repos remain at /private/tmp/rebar-a1-measure.H0rPNy; the durable evidence is this exact protocol, inputs, object sizes, formula, and result plus the prior ticket comment's ordered SHA list."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785699068165427001,"uuid":"ed9ae5d9-b3c6-4b73-8542-22dbb28b43ae"}